            <ArticleTitle>Fatal Deer Tick Virus Infection in Maine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1043-1046</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1093/cid/cix435</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Deer tick virus (DTV), a genetic variant (lineage II) of Powassan virus, is a rare cause of encephalitis in North America. We report a fatal case of DTV encephalitis following a documented bite from an Ixodes scapularis tick and the erythema migrans rash associated with Lyme disease.</AbstractText>
